  "name": "Act2Intention: A Benchmark For Developing Active Mobile Agents Through Inferring User Intention from GUI Actions",
  "notes": "The benchmark combines real and generated trajectory material. Opportune intervention timing and real-user acceptance are stated limitations. Section 4.2.2 specifies Android emulator instances for generated action trajectories. No results were independently reproduced. Basis: complete retained abstract and source-reviewed sections of the exact-version paper (3 Task definition; 4.1 Raw data collection; 4.2 Trajectory construction; 7 Limitations and future directions); not an entire-paper reading or reproduction claim.",
  "published_at": "2026-08-14",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "Introduces intention understanding, prediction, and confirmed execution tasks over mobile GUI trajectories, with a proactive agent combining personalized intention models and experience-guided actions.",
